  "evidence": "In Switzerland, the requirement for an L-permit (or work permit) depends on the type of work, the duration of the stay, and the nationality of the individual. For short-term assignments, such as a two-week assignment, the rules can vary based on the specific circumstances. Generally, for stays of up to 90 days within a 180-day period, certain nationalities may be exempt from needing a work permit for short-term work assignments, especially if the work is related to a specific project or task."
